        "content": "Each card below was written from one document, in answer to the same question. Sort the cards into groups.\n\nQuestion: When did the Women's Strike take place?\n\nCard 1 (from document 1)\n  entity: Icelandic women\n  sense: not stated\n  answer: 24 October 1975\n  as of: not stated\n  evidence: \"On 24 October 1975, Icelandic women did not go to their paid jobs nor did they do any housework or child-rearing at home.\"\nCard 2 (from document 2)\n  entity: 90 % of women in Iceland\n  sense: not stated\n  answer: 24 October 1975\n  as of: not stated\n  evidence: \"But Vigdis insists she would never have been president had it not been for the events of one sunny day - 24 October 1975 - when 90 % of women in the country decided to demonstrate their importance by going on strike.\"\nCard 3 (from document 3)\n  entity: Icelandic women\n  sense: not stated\n  answer: 24 October 1975\n  as of: not stated\n  evidence: \"On 24 October 1975 , Icelandic women went on strike for the day to `` demonstrate the indispensable work of women for Iceland 's economy and society '' [ 1 ] and to `` protest wage discrepancy and unfair employment practices '' .\"\nCard 4 (from document 4)\n  entity: Spanish women\n  sense: 2018 Spanish women's strike\n  answer: March 8, 2018\n  as of: not stated\n  evidence: \"On March 8, 2018, International Women's Day, Spanish women went on strike for the day to denounce sexual discrimination, domestic violence and the wage gap.\"\nCard 5 (from document 5)\n  entity: Women Strike for Peace\n  sense: not stated\n  answer: January 1962\n  as of: not stated\n  evidence: \"In January 1962, Berkeley Women\"\n\nSort in three layers:\n1. Entity. Cards about the same real-world thing go together. A shared name is not enough, because different people, places and works can have the same name: go by the identifying details (what kind of thing, role, place, years, other names). Cards that describe one thing in different words go together. Cards with the same identifying details go together even when their answers differ.\n2. Sense. Inside an entity, cards about the same event, edition, version, condition, place or measure go together. Cards whose sense is \"not stated\" go in a sense named \"not stated\".\n3. Answer. Inside a sense, cards with compatible answers go together: the same answer in other words or at another precision, such as \"December 2009\" and \"18 December 2009\". Answers that differ go in separate groups, whichever you believe is right.\n\nReply with JSON only, in this form, where each list of numbers is one group of cards with compatible answers:\n{\"entities\": [{\"name\": \"\", \"senses\": [{\"name\": \"\", \"answers\": [[1, 2], [3]]}]}], \"uncertain\": []}\n\n\"name\" of an entity: its full name with the details that identify it.\n\"uncertain\": the numbers of the cards that could belong to more than one entity.\nEvery card number appears exactly once under \"answers\"."
